# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
# Source of truth for the seeded interview question bank. Edit here, then run:
#   python3 supabase/seed/interview_bank.py > supabase/migrations/0069_seed_interview_bank.sql
#
# Why this is written by hand rather than generated by a model:
#
# `interview_question_bank` is a cache keyed on (role, session_type,
# difficulty). The first student to ask for a combination pays one of their
# three daily AI actions and everybody after them gets it free. It has been
# empty since it was created, so every student has been paying for questions
# somebody else already generated.
#
# Seeding it makes interview practice free from the day this lands. Writing the
# questions by hand rather than generating them once also means they are
# reviewable in git, they do not drift when a model changes, and they can be
# specific to the market these students are actually interviewing in — the same
# reason the 261 roadmap tasks were written this way.
#
# Nine questions per role, tagged easy/medium/hard, composed into the three
# difficulty sets. Writing 9 and composing 3 sets of 5 gives better questions
# than writing 15 mediocre ones, and a question that appears in two tiers is
# not a defect: an interviewer asks the same thing of a nervous student and a
# confident one.

E, M, H = "easy", "medium", "hard"

# Behavioural questions are the same whatever the role — nobody asks a
